[{:db/id "q-161358/selection/ef4df2f9504c4e97415d6b713328740d90b21b25095022173eaaba5b61b72300" :answer/id #uuid "f9e56533-3fe1-5d55-a002-6d2b32d46769" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4u+7v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161358/selection/0034fb5c17c2082a74b830cbafe62b1ce4ef28ff6d8107f40ad6ee09fb32ae0f" :answer/id #uuid "bd0cf11e-e153-51a9-af49-de25ba7fa6e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8u-7v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161358/selection/7d689009290eac697665cbd104e19fb1e7dd58e262abc66f9ee86c1cac0cc729" :answer/id #uuid "c30fbe04-36e7-5f57-a6d5-bb9697700be0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7u-8v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161358/selection/db1daf91662e5675817f38f908c343dc47fd1f574cca9dec627395ff5bc7bcd3" :answer/id #uuid "234d6cb8-0668-596f-90aa-930da9fc6f9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7u+4v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161358/selection/e73a736b0601903b7ce31477a7b4949ee948be5697ca2c214ab6c5ce6d69d6c6" :answer/id #uuid "9ac550db-b4b3-5747-80f9-9e4006ac560c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7u+8v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161358/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b45c99f-ef17-5b3f-8651-d9ffb4882eb8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161358/selection/db1daf91662e5675817f38f908c343dc47fd1f574cca9dec627395ff5bc7bcd3" :answer-field/choices ["q-161358/selection/ef4df2f9504c4e97415d6b713328740d90b21b25095022173eaaba5b61b72300" "q-161358/selection/0034fb5c17c2082a74b830cbafe62b1ce4ef28ff6d8107f40ad6ee09fb32ae0f" "q-161358/selection/7d689009290eac697665cbd104e19fb1e7dd58e262abc66f9ee86c1cac0cc729" "q-161358/selection/db1daf91662e5675817f38f908c343dc47fd1f574cca9dec627395ff5bc7bcd3" "q-161358/selection/e73a736b0601903b7ce31477a7b4949ee948be5697ca2c214ab6c5ce6d69d6c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161358" :question/id #uuid "e117b73c-5d7e-50a5-8413-ceb336d67fad" :question/math-academy-id "q-161358" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,-y,\\,2x⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=3x-2y$ for $0\\le x\\le 5$ and $-3\\le y\\le 3.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,3u-2v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 5,\\,-3\\le v\\le 3}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,3⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\,-y,\\,2x⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=3u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨3u-2v,\\,-v,\\,2u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3u-2v,\\,-v,\\,2u⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(3u-2v)\\cdot (-3)+(-v)\\cdot (2)+2u\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-9u+6v-2v+2u \\\\  & =-7u+4v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,-y,\\,2x⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-7u+4v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}(-7u+4v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161358/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a3486150-b3c2-5faf-99d5-b42ced350996"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161358"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161359/selection/7159a960144a256245bf8387c88bea2e4b5e1b1ff6bb2a0b76dd9d85aee7518b" :answer/id #uuid "4e42b90a-18f6-53a4-abab-a1666210e21f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161359/selection/c193e136e97cc4b0206137d7bc339daf600e96eec10a71c0cea8f06e3982d36b" :answer/id #uuid "75ced647-35e7-5373-a62b-6ff965d54d94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161359/selection/da772ca5bbe7da853d2e6a3756f6ee2df1b44d18f238029ee5ac1fbea666e3c2" :answer/id #uuid "bf5f7b7d-f47a-53ad-bd26-c188a65c8f0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(u-v)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161359/selection/c3d20475246818166b7bd614ae7dc243ccd19389acb8115a1367398a47870d0d" :answer/id #uuid "5345d599-a095-5b2c-aead-7491bb47eeac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(u+v)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161359/selection/eaae3272142bda04bf332ba57a7cee56c8de50819ed615ab69dfe74979a7eb07" :answer/id #uuid "8f3b6e73-f684-53a0-9c93-ef870a497c18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{2}+uv-{v}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161359/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b601ef07-a888-5d6b-8b21-55e4b2e63821" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161359/selection/7159a960144a256245bf8387c88bea2e4b5e1b1ff6bb2a0b76dd9d85aee7518b" :answer-field/choices ["q-161359/selection/7159a960144a256245bf8387c88bea2e4b5e1b1ff6bb2a0b76dd9d85aee7518b" "q-161359/selection/c193e136e97cc4b0206137d7bc339daf600e96eec10a71c0cea8f06e3982d36b" "q-161359/selection/da772ca5bbe7da853d2e6a3756f6ee2df1b44d18f238029ee5ac1fbea666e3c2" "q-161359/selection/c3d20475246818166b7bd614ae7dc243ccd19389acb8115a1367398a47870d0d" "q-161359/selection/eaae3272142bda04bf332ba57a7cee56c8de50819ed615ab69dfe74979a7eb07"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161359" :question/id #uuid "d5e1155b-c484-5f31-a815-946d2d63d6df" :question/math-academy-id "q-161359" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨zy,\\,xz,\\,xy⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x-y$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u-v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨zy,\\,xz,\\,xy⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=u-v} \\\\  & =⟨(u-v)v,\\,(u-v)u,\\,uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨(u-v)v,\\,(u-v)u,\\,uv⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u-v)v\\cdot (-1)+(u-v)u\\cdot (1)+uv\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-uv+{v}^{2}+{u}^{2}-uv+uv \\\\  & ={u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨zy,\\,xz,\\,xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161359/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a3486150-b3c2-5faf-99d5-b42ced350996"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161359"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161462/selection/4f489e7f30a19a495b73ffefb52314ff163b93334452d5d0703d3ab9034c62b2" :answer/id #uuid "c0ef8dfe-6b96-5b46-84ce-48b2876b9d42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3u-3v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161462/selection/82af36f06f8afc5c7ca9e46f344c7bdbc2a8ee35b13e9ea637e52592d183f724" :answer/id #uuid "8cfb5b3f-9159-5176-9c51-c2974bf9d755" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3v+u" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161462/selection/bb149e5b980604047e93d551e11f654bf68d943b8e261b2025bff22b8287a622" :answer/id #uuid "8f7593f4-6fdc-52aa-9627-0eca001368ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2u+v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161462/selection/9817c5a7ccdb4f217f637df192700ed065deccc1bf48920632063056e1b18a39" :answer/id #uuid "a8b96d65-bea2-5f56-803f-d1a5e2977788" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2u-3v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161462/selection/ee49020ed7e2c5dde184096f48327217179caf6645165b157bc7243886f74426" :answer/id #uuid "d8bfa992-9fe5-5679-83c1-39ae9da2e6c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u+2v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161462/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a6d80c6-99af-544c-9507-dfcb6be489f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161462/selection/4f489e7f30a19a495b73ffefb52314ff163b93334452d5d0703d3ab9034c62b2" :answer-field/choices ["q-161462/selection/4f489e7f30a19a495b73ffefb52314ff163b93334452d5d0703d3ab9034c62b2" "q-161462/selection/82af36f06f8afc5c7ca9e46f344c7bdbc2a8ee35b13e9ea637e52592d183f724" "q-161462/selection/bb149e5b980604047e93d551e11f654bf68d943b8e261b2025bff22b8287a622" "q-161462/selection/9817c5a7ccdb4f217f637df192700ed065deccc1bf48920632063056e1b18a39" "q-161462/selection/ee49020ed7e2c5dde184096f48327217179caf6645165b157bc7243886f74426"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161462" :question/id #uuid "26abce92-8c74-52ee-98e4-e9b7dcf9dd05" :question/math-academy-id "q-161462" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,y+2z,\\,2x-y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=y-x$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,v-u⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\,y+2z,\\,2x-y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=v-u} \\\\  & =⟨v-u,\\,v+2(v-u),\\,2u-v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨v-u,\\,3v-2u,\\,2u-v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨v-u,\\,3v-2u,\\,2u-v⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(v-u)\\cdot 1+(3v-2u)\\cdot (-1)+(2u-v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =v-u-3v+2u+2u-v \\\\  & =3u-3v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,y+2z,\\,2x-y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3u-3v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(3u-3v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161462/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a3486150-b3c2-5faf-99d5-b42ced350996"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161462"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161357/selection/6e59713f6b879702b491b97312323568e2b8ba7e2b05cbe3c2cdd120cb8436fd" :answer/id #uuid "67588143-02de-53f0-b980-baa26f9862f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3uv" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161357/selection/e1ba13e972f703b9c92836ec51aa344b6aa57627d23a0d26323d3f3acbe15d3e" :answer/id #uuid "7ceacbe4-6df6-519f-836a-74082fbb7fba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5u-6v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161357/selection/95e55e09c8fd088b369b94477d725ae2e75cac1e692891f1ba56c531a79712c4" :answer/id #uuid "029bc8ee-4638-5446-a3f8-85252b1aa123" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11uv" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161357/selection/3483a8b73bef95f967c3ea109c98bfe9d90a6bbf466824ffab52b308a887400a" :answer/id #uuid "895d8329-0265-5a31-8d65-e8c863ca6468" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2u+v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161357/selection/b457ef847266cf0f37ae72a63d53032673dd9a313030dd351d996287f2cfe925" :answer/id #uuid "27574249-a18c-5a11-b918-e4c7fbc908d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u+v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161357/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c1ec354e-0321-5a3a-a13f-ddd5c3b7ba3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161357/selection/e1ba13e972f703b9c92836ec51aa344b6aa57627d23a0d26323d3f3acbe15d3e" :answer-field/choices ["q-161357/selection/6e59713f6b879702b491b97312323568e2b8ba7e2b05cbe3c2cdd120cb8436fd" "q-161357/selection/e1ba13e972f703b9c92836ec51aa344b6aa57627d23a0d26323d3f3acbe15d3e" "q-161357/selection/95e55e09c8fd088b369b94477d725ae2e75cac1e692891f1ba56c531a79712c4" "q-161357/selection/3483a8b73bef95f967c3ea109c98bfe9d90a6bbf466824ffab52b308a887400a" "q-161357/selection/b457ef847266cf0f37ae72a63d53032673dd9a313030dd351d996287f2cfe925"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161357" :question/id #uuid "eec4b66c-4af6-5b13-942b-337cb7b8732a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161357" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x+y,\\,2x-y,\\,x+z⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2x-2y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2u-2v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x+y,\\,2x-y,\\,x+z⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨u+v,\\,2u-v,\\,u+(2u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u+v,\\,2u-v,\\,3u-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u+v,\\,2u-v,\\,3u-2v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u+v)\\cdot (-2)+(2u-v)\\cdot (2)+(3u-2v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2u-2v+4u-2v+3u-2v \\\\  & =5u-6v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x+y,\\,2x-y,\\,x+z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5u-6v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(5u-6v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161357/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a3486150-b3c2-5faf-99d5-b42ced350996"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161357"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161441/selection/ecb08c557f7f1c243f6f0e03806b535d3214f2d888fe452940b5225c9f4e7fe4" :answer/id #uuid "fe7180ed-3b36-5c49-a46b-f8a903bee072" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2u+7v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161441/selection/3483a8b73bef95f967c3ea109c98bfe9d90a6bbf466824ffab52b308a887400a" :answer/id #uuid "e28d969d-0e16-5169-8cbb-bbd0268c7286" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2u+v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161441/selection/d32b17a53d022e2632ef7757059045b2c2e993e8c0d1c93c6ba9969ddb694252" :answer/id #uuid "cd8c1820-28fb-5a9f-9cd1-66a0c1517b80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2u+4v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161441/selection/d5ff5f2272b28579d0bbab4d23af312f24bb073d3bbe5efc152a6fa5490f7e24" :answer/id #uuid "1be10ec9-2b08-553e-9c3b-a0af8c587898" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4u+v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161441/selection/6c55c0727cb1a6c06542dbc527271df43bb6eb3ddfc3ec64c90a78972950f06c" :answer/id #uuid "82170582-9157-565d-aa01-985627b175da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4v-u" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161441/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b2e121ee-9563-5425-8c9d-e1134482fb08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161441/selection/ecb08c557f7f1c243f6f0e03806b535d3214f2d888fe452940b5225c9f4e7fe4" :answer-field/choices ["q-161441/selection/ecb08c557f7f1c243f6f0e03806b535d3214f2d888fe452940b5225c9f4e7fe4" "q-161441/selection/3483a8b73bef95f967c3ea109c98bfe9d90a6bbf466824ffab52b308a887400a" "q-161441/selection/d32b17a53d022e2632ef7757059045b2c2e993e8c0d1c93c6ba9969ddb694252" "q-161441/selection/d5ff5f2272b28579d0bbab4d23af312f24bb073d3bbe5efc152a6fa5490f7e24" "q-161441/selection/6c55c0727cb1a6c06542dbc527271df43bb6eb3ddfc3ec64c90a78972950f06c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161441" :question/id #uuid "add8b593-befe-5cd7-803b-d2901a2c8bd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-161441" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x,\\,y-z,\\,x+y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x-2y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $-1\\le y\\le 1.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u-2v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,-1\\le v\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x,\\,y-z,\\,x+y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨u,\\,v-(u-2v),\\,u+v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u,\\,3v-u,\\,u+v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u,\\,3v-u,\\,u+v⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =u\\cdot (-1)+(3v-u)\\cdot 2+(u+v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-u+6v-2u+u+v \\\\  & =-2u+7v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,y-z,\\,x+y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-2u+7v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-2u+7v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161441/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a3486150-b3c2-5faf-99d5-b42ced350996"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161441"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161453/selection/3e9594dd3c01dff6ec712daaca147eb881fc0e6b18cccacf528838e3885b41c2" :answer/id #uuid "7e210066-3bb3-50cf-82ca-dbf97dcab830" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2P$ and $R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161453/selection/1527e045928cf048ab3c31bc2a994ca24d6eacf9941af91d0850ae97c4ef277a" :answer/id #uuid "2da9f05a-16db-547b-8a66-a53dafc6f4a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-2P$ and $2R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161453/selection/4991b41ff9a1f2140d217518847833e066189ee00d4c2793b7a9d3bf8a591555" :answer/id #uuid "c79d9827-7ae6-5324-9376-7a92d886de32" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2P$ and $-2R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161453/selection/9bc47d99621d0bbcf97ca6fae716e63f789a11737e8e3ab06c8ef99d30a7f358" :answer/id #uuid "7eaf58cf-09bd-5063-8f81-9e32fb6f4faf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $-2R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161453/selection/0dedb59aa374085c0f32f11b97856c46fc2cf9f2b20519d2889045593905aa47" :answer/id #uuid "b2de53b8-58ac-5e62-b156-56a4470cd220" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161453/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf8e3e5d-a9f7-5b68-83a0-12a09c7ce5e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161453/selection/3e9594dd3c01dff6ec712daaca147eb881fc0e6b18cccacf528838e3885b41c2" :answer-field/choices ["q-161453/selection/3e9594dd3c01dff6ec712daaca147eb881fc0e6b18cccacf528838e3885b41c2" "q-161453/selection/1527e045928cf048ab3c31bc2a994ca24d6eacf9941af91d0850ae97c4ef277a" "q-161453/selection/4991b41ff9a1f2140d217518847833e066189ee00d4c2793b7a9d3bf8a591555" "q-161453/selection/9bc47d99621d0bbcf97ca6fae716e63f789a11737e8e3ab06c8ef99d30a7f358" "q-161453/selection/0dedb59aa374085c0f32f11b97856c46fc2cf9f2b20519d2889045593905aa47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161453" :question/id #uuid "de61fa00-8c2a-5649-8bdc-5bd36078a722" :question/math-academy-id "q-161453" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $y=-{x}^{2}z$ for $(x,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(\\,xz+Q+\\,{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?\n\n*Hint: The orientation of $S$ should be chosen such that the unit normal vector has a positive  $j$-component.*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $y=-{x}^{2}z,$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,z)=⟨x,\\,-{x}^{2}z,z⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,-2xz,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,-{x}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -2xz & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{x}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨-2xz,\\,-1,\\,-{x}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, notice that the $j$-component is negative. Therefore, we select the normal vector that points in the *opposite* direction:\n\n$$\n{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{x}^{′}=-{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′}=⟨2xz,\\,1,\\,{x}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,z))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,R\\,⟩\\cdot ⟨2xz,\\,1,\\,{x}^{2}⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2P\\,xz+Q+R\\,{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-161453/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55cd2fdb-4cae-5f0b-bea0-e845d51190e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161453"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161463/selection/32c59be4107772ec048c7f4ad1386a03977a160d5c51a9d93b1cb4f936a7f895" :answer/id #uuid "9e8d7573-3013-5fd1-9500-8c0b8bca3558" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$∂x$ and $∂z$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161463/selection/65177cc40635859ee8ee479d0f23d83a4e02b6edd6469381c62aee473e2b54ff" :answer/id #uuid "ba4c6d01-fa5d-5cfe-953e-d6b8896fbcb4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$∂y$ and $∂z$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161463/selection/1874cb4b13d2152ca2b7231b546e3c9c806e410e543beefdf124270fee882300" :answer/id #uuid "569c0f26-cf3e-508d-8d27-ebf9af1cae3b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$∂z$ and $∂x$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161463/selection/a8cd0e828d56933080f0c934926527f00118d30be88bd1eb8b6d59158280b81c" :answer/id #uuid "21f597a5-dcea-50ad-9bfe-82a1e6e48695" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$∂y$ and $∂x$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161463/selection/7fc8826ee1211a7af48fd0c0130c2e2fb4533c62b46e2d484bbf6ca03cab501a" :answer/id #uuid "e2f82876-b91b-5aa8-b80f-079520703f97" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$∂x$ and $∂y$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161463/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "06b828bd-aa53-5e28-874f-d3df66b2c822" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161463/selection/7fc8826ee1211a7af48fd0c0130c2e2fb4533c62b46e2d484bbf6ca03cab501a" :answer-field/choices ["q-161463/selection/32c59be4107772ec048c7f4ad1386a03977a160d5c51a9d93b1cb4f936a7f895" "q-161463/selection/65177cc40635859ee8ee479d0f23d83a4e02b6edd6469381c62aee473e2b54ff" "q-161463/selection/1874cb4b13d2152ca2b7231b546e3c9c806e410e543beefdf124270fee882300" "q-161463/selection/a8cd0e828d56933080f0c934926527f00118d30be88bd1eb8b6d59158280b81c" "q-161463/selection/7fc8826ee1211a7af48fd0c0130c2e2fb4533c62b46e2d484bbf6ca03cab501a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161463" :question/id #uuid "b2128236-dd4e-5cec-8d28-c07554df0f5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-161463" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{}-Q\\frac{∂g}{}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $z=g(x,y),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,g(x,y)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂x}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\frac{∂g}{∂x} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\end{aligned}|=⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161463/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55cd2fdb-4cae-5f0b-bea0-e845d51190e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161463"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-161189"] :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂g}{∂x}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $z=g(x,y),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,g(x,y)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂x}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\frac{∂g}{∂x} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\end{aligned}|=⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}+(-Q\\,)\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-161455/selection/adfed47a55c97fa62c629b2ea9d9164e879251e14e11ca48b75971e47318d78f" :answer/id #uuid "9134eb87-01af-5ce6-adc5-66f87917337b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-2P$ and $6R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161455/selection/4d5270e188cd4fd9a3fffa677eceb1961a8d47f1872b4ceaae0bc279a58034cd" :answer/id #uuid "f4b27aed-2259-584c-9979-e5ddd0cfc520" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $-6R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161455/selection/0dedb59aa374085c0f32f11b97856c46fc2cf9f2b20519d2889045593905aa47" :answer/id #uuid "33ec83ac-a887-56f8-add7-1cad8c103351" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161455/selection/02fe04009804a6122da58f387f8fa07385b3fb99471956df098843d4821378b5" :answer/id #uuid "ec908d62-05a3-5244-809e-fc6e3064645d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-2R$ and $-2P$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161455/selection/8193b1433f85412839082aee9920d38991c11d2250319ef5dad19da17d981021" :answer/id #uuid "76aaf53f-e992-5281-b1b6-afeb1c63a0b5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-2P$ and $-R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161455/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bfd91811-e57f-576d-9abb-213a83b76ef5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161455/selection/adfed47a55c97fa62c629b2ea9d9164e879251e14e11ca48b75971e47318d78f" :answer-field/choices ["q-161455/selection/adfed47a55c97fa62c629b2ea9d9164e879251e14e11ca48b75971e47318d78f" "q-161455/selection/4d5270e188cd4fd9a3fffa677eceb1961a8d47f1872b4ceaae0bc279a58034cd" "q-161455/selection/0dedb59aa374085c0f32f11b97856c46fc2cf9f2b20519d2889045593905aa47" "q-161455/selection/02fe04009804a6122da58f387f8fa07385b3fb99471956df098843d4821378b5" "q-161455/selection/8193b1433f85412839082aee9920d38991c11d2250319ef5dad19da17d981021"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161455" :question/id #uuid "75438633-2fed-5dc6-8f93-bd3571d872a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-161455" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $y=2x{z}^{3}$ for $(x,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(\\,{z}^{3}+Q-\\,x{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?\n\n*Hint: The orientation of $S$ should be chosen such that the unit normal vector has a positive  $j$-component.*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $y=2x{z}^{3},$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,z)=⟨x,\\,2x{z}^{3},z⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,2{z}^{3},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,6x{z}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2{z}^{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6x{z}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨2{z}^{3},\\,-1,\\,6x{z}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, notice that the $j$-component is negative. Therefore, we select the normal vector that points in the *opposite* direction:\n\n$$\n{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{x}^{′}=-{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′}=⟨-2{z}^{3},\\,1,\\,-6x{z}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,z))\\cdot ({r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{x}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,R\\,⟩\\cdot ⟨-2{z}^{3},\\,1,\\,-6x{z}^{2}⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-2P\\,{z}^{3}+Q-6R\\,x{z}^{2}\\,)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-161455/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55cd2fdb-4cae-5f0b-bea0-e845d51190e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161455"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161456/selection/2ce8d7a5410daaf396065dec63f4265d4dfa6b5d0b6a613be6c6fc7a25e7da2a" :answer/id #uuid "ec080afb-a715-5b8f-8b41-937e68f1b78e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ and $-2R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161456/selection/93b31c72efe8d7d91c68a9b7e85bfc04960592e8bc80aa010fbab81b45e4d96f" :answer/id #uuid "6f77a4b2-37a2-54df-bd98-e6cead745515" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-2Q$ and $R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161456/selection/cf846cb991edbb431d8d4abd71027ad6d9083027c5b3bb96fc9a6e3e86e6ffa8" :answer/id #uuid "70bb5f01-8984-5070-ad1f-7279aee2bec5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-Q$ and $-R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161456/selection/0f29f08412d4b986b57bf0aae0503785525e4eebc5190d9bcb19656fdff62df2" :answer/id #uuid "3b774026-5c53-5737-9f8a-7141cddcfbe8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-2Q$ and $-2R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161456/selection/8d9516eec434b0ae312a1a256b94851b8f42f29d7c2717da2ca6b2734350b991" :answer/id #uuid "da184f08-1756-54e5-ab72-dcf9863b57d1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161456/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "28f71383-d867-5deb-88e2-2186eb746120" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161456/selection/0f29f08412d4b986b57bf0aae0503785525e4eebc5190d9bcb19656fdff62df2" :answer-field/choices ["q-161456/selection/2ce8d7a5410daaf396065dec63f4265d4dfa6b5d0b6a613be6c6fc7a25e7da2a" "q-161456/selection/93b31c72efe8d7d91c68a9b7e85bfc04960592e8bc80aa010fbab81b45e4d96f" "q-161456/selection/cf846cb991edbb431d8d4abd71027ad6d9083027c5b3bb96fc9a6e3e86e6ffa8" "q-161456/selection/0f29f08412d4b986b57bf0aae0503785525e4eebc5190d9bcb19656fdff62df2" "q-161456/selection/8d9516eec434b0ae312a1a256b94851b8f42f29d7c2717da2ca6b2734350b991"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161456" :question/id #uuid "1848d1e1-e808-5cfe-8698-af501778b472" :question/math-academy-id "q-161456" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $x=2yz$ for $(y,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(P+\\,z+\\,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $x=2yz,$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(y,z)=⟨2yz,\\,y,\\,z⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨2z,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨2y,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2z & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2y & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨1,\\,-2z,\\,-2y⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(y,z))\\cdot ({r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-2z,\\,-2y⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(P+(\\,-2Q)\\,z+(\\,-2R)\\,y\\,)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161456/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55cd2fdb-4cae-5f0b-bea0-e845d51190e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161456"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161539/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "2e66930b-da2a-561c-bbad-58ba4cb49ed2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161539/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "12fd981d-e3ee-5461-9b0b-b0aa84905509" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161539/selection/6acadda2cf01d7393af5cf150300ca180189308ad197cceffca549e1b6e5368c" :answer/id #uuid "ec5cf4ca-1ed0-56af-a739-2e16a03d83f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi -1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161539/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" :answer/id #uuid "dd6a3bd1-8f7a-554e-ab87-c4b76cc69e44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161539/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "515ffcb7-e532-5100-8482-a11fe24009d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161539/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0abd0d35-115c-5f41-b432-0c479a59b6e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161539/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer-field/choices ["q-161539/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-161539/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-161539/selection/6acadda2cf01d7393af5cf150300ca180189308ad197cceffca549e1b6e5368c" "q-161539/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" "q-161539/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161539" :question/id #uuid "82c8b088-1d00-54ec-a79c-4ebe46ed74fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-161539" :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨{cos}^{2}⁡(xy),\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(xy),\\,1⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(xy)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $-x\\le y\\le 0.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(xy))=\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡(xy)} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(xy))=\\frac{x}{{cos}^{2}⁡(xy)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨{cos}^{2}⁡(xy),\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(xy),\\,1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨{cos}^{2}⁡(xy),\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(xy),\\,1⟩{|}_{z=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(xy)} \\\\  & =⟨{{{cos}^{2}⁡(xy)}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{{cos}^{2}⁡(xy)}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{1}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨{cos}^{2}⁡(xy),\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(xy),\\,1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-({cos}^{2}⁡(xy))\\cdot (\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡(xy)})-({cos}^{2}⁡(xy))\\cdot (\\frac{x}{{cos}^{2}⁡(xy)})+1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y-x+1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-x}^{0}(-y-x+1)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-xy+y]}_{y=-x}^{y=0}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-{x}^{2}+x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-161539/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaa6b152-86d3-5f96-8a94-57f86a17a84d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161539"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161382/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "0baf64c5-7e07-5347-8680-80cb51599cb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161382/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "ad83af97-9017-57bb-9f65-e18bbd2825a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161382/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" :answer/id #uuid "952d95d9-8aa5-5bc7-bc8c-da85adeb714c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161382/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "b32ef309-8942-56ac-a581-0a9c61b1957f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161382/selection/53a62adc469f7106cfcc253972af70d0b351ee4c505c92859749c553ee85bd38" :answer/id #uuid "9eca2258-5d3f-5591-ab3a-973d49b954ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161382/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cee24689-b113-59c2-8c30-d43c5df11e3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161382/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-161382/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-161382/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-161382/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" "q-161382/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-161382/selection/53a62adc469f7106cfcc253972af70d0b351ee4c505c92859749c553ee85bd38"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161382" :question/id #uuid "fbae2fc2-a596-53ce-90bd-68baf53dc180" :question/math-academy-id "q-161382" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨-x,\\,-y,\\,xyz⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=2x+y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x+y)=2 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x+y)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨-x,\\,-y,\\,xyz⟩{|}_{z=2x+y} \\\\  & =⟨-x,\\,-y,\\,xy(2x+y)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{{-x}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{-y}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{xy(2x+y)}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨-x,\\,-y,\\,xyz⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-(-x)\\cdot 2-(-y)\\cdot (1)+xy(2x+y))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2x+y+2{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2x+y+2{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2xy+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{x{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2x+\\frac{1}{2}+{x}^{2}+\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+\\frac{7x}{3}+\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{7{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{x}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{7}{6}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161382/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaa6b152-86d3-5f96-8a94-57f86a17a84d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161382"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161542/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "8aaf199e-0f93-5e6a-870b-971667c0a528" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161542/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "5d7bed59-1433-5e38-8ea7-596a72e057e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161542/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer/id #uuid "077ff43c-bfbf-5468-8129-239c3abca86a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161542/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "e4d83609-526c-51fb-aaee-be20995a4c33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161542/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "9e532718-e7c0-5570-b344-4c58fb0f8cdf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161542/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd28223f-6e99-5141-ae8b-dec23fdd0b6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161542/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer-field/choices ["q-161542/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-161542/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" "q-161542/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" "q-161542/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-161542/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161542" :question/id #uuid "da6e081d-b676-514f-be3e-16d3d87d2d54" :question/math-academy-id "q-161542" :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨x+y,\\,y-x,\\,z⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $-1\\le y\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2x \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨x+y,\\,y-x,\\,z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨x+y,\\,y-x,\\,z⟩{|}_{z=1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨{{x+y}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{y-x}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x+y,\\,y-x,\\,z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-(x+y)\\cdot (2x)-(y-x)\\cdot (2y)+1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-2{x}^{2}-2xy-2{y}^{2}+2xy+1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(1-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[y-{x}^{2}y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=-1}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[(1-{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3})-(-1+{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3})]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(2-2{x}^{2}-\\frac{2}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2x-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}x]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(2-\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2}{3})-(-2+\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-161542/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaa6b152-86d3-5f96-8a94-57f86a17a84d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161542"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161476/selection/f0bcd52c0538033e428af5bb39ffc16253ef2b5f16b014192904f74f959202ea" :answer/id #uuid "84181d8b-8c0c-5d8e-b782-089c6f629222" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e-\\frac{19}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161476/selection/685868e3f9895320192fc81fba3013434a88d0da2bd101e2415e4bd9aa0b5293" :answer/id #uuid "9945d00a-4b77-5e91-9427-d7b754ddeaba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2}+e-\\frac{19}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161476/selection/53cf6cc56ccfc69e82857c0937d315a778599585cfc945ee92766f39fea86423" :answer/id #uuid "3f68826c-0a17-5de5-8937-8426a8756fb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2}-\\frac{17}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161476/selection/f1ca83cfb83fd7780b58c7b73a74ccd5d5d9d5707e27246648ea299af5b2213a" :answer/id #uuid "a905245b-51aa-59e6-b1e2-fb533ed39746" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e-\\frac{15}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161476/selection/fea5ac79e1324b707b888c0edd4109aee18e7b13da6b628aa9ad9ea158b6c090" :answer/id #uuid "5bb5c0f0-d2d2-53c2-a212-899acd8bb040" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2}-e-\\frac{13}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161476/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9575cc63-04a7-58c6-8a88-560cd38e3955" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161476/selection/f0bcd52c0538033e428af5bb39ffc16253ef2b5f16b014192904f74f959202ea" :answer-field/choices ["q-161476/selection/f0bcd52c0538033e428af5bb39ffc16253ef2b5f16b014192904f74f959202ea" "q-161476/selection/685868e3f9895320192fc81fba3013434a88d0da2bd101e2415e4bd9aa0b5293" "q-161476/selection/53cf6cc56ccfc69e82857c0937d315a778599585cfc945ee92766f39fea86423" "q-161476/selection/f1ca83cfb83fd7780b58c7b73a74ccd5d5d9d5707e27246648ea299af5b2213a" "q-161476/selection/fea5ac79e1324b707b888c0edd4109aee18e7b13da6b628aa9ad9ea158b6c090"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161476" :question/id #uuid "682d2ef7-9cff-5a52-921d-70cd49bbb080" :question/math-academy-id "q-161476" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨\\frac{1}{z},\\,\\frac{xy}{z},\\,z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z={e}^{x-y}$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le x.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}{e}^{x-y}={e}^{x-y} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}{e}^{x-y}=-{e}^{x-y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨\\frac{1}{z},\\,\\frac{xy}{z},\\,z⟩{|}_{z={e}^{x-y}} \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{-(x-y)},\\,xy{e}^{-(x-y)},\\,{e}^{x-y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{{{e}^{y-x}}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{xy{e}^{y-x}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{{e}^{x-y}}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨\\frac{1}{z},\\,\\frac{xy}{z},\\,z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-{e}^{y-x}\\cdot {e}^{x-y}-(xy{e}^{y-x})\\cdot (-{e}^{x-y})+{e}^{x-y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-1+xy+{e}^{x-y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}(-1+xy+{e}^{x-y})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-y+\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{2}-{e}^{x-y}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}-1+{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{8}-x+{e}^{x}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{8}-1+e)-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{19}{8}+e\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161476/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaa6b152-86d3-5f96-8a94-57f86a17a84d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161476"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161481/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "544f945e-1948-54fa-9a69-6265f16fee7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161481/selection/1c4b980c3123fbd8f0c887e499a8833bafbffb834bb3982ebb6af4c39796469c" :answer/id #uuid "89607af9-a96f-5710-950d-43d5b27cd967" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161481/selection/1ac75f82a6cfc040418219e106e227323565cf59e85a378bbbc0c948329befb9" :answer/id #uuid "656ea4bb-04c7-53fa-ae19-e02f1bb423db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi +\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161481/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "57146f5c-731b-5aeb-918e-8bfe4c3afbde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161481/selection/7f76a5c9cbc54754b52bb6319f7eb7703d4f1e705f3b39679d566372ebcc5af8" :answer/id #uuid "d26f0f79-3b55-5d36-a0f4-e27e53b47ba8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi +\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161481/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e60bf7b-4f92-588e-8cc2-c224f19216da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161481/selection/1c4b980c3123fbd8f0c887e499a8833bafbffb834bb3982ebb6af4c39796469c" :answer-field/choices ["q-161481/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-161481/selection/1c4b980c3123fbd8f0c887e499a8833bafbffb834bb3982ebb6af4c39796469c" "q-161481/selection/1ac75f82a6cfc040418219e106e227323565cf59e85a378bbbc0c948329befb9" "q-161481/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-161481/selection/7f76a5c9cbc54754b52bb6319f7eb7703d4f1e705f3b39679d566372ebcc5af8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161481" :question/id #uuid "75f60136-1ae9-5f0b-8a88-b99b9aa1fce7" :question/math-academy-id "q-161481" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨1,\\,0,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)$ for $-\\pi \\le x\\le 0$ and $-x\\le y\\le 0.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y) \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,y⟩{|}_{z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)} \\\\  & =⟨{{1}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{0}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{y}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨1,\\,0,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-1\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y))-0\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y))+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}{\\int }_{-x}^{0}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=-x}^{y=0}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+0)-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}]}_{-\\pi }^{0} \\\\  & =0-(-0+(-\\pi )-\\frac{(-\\pi )^{3}}{6}) \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161481/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaa6b152-86d3-5f96-8a94-57f86a17a84d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161481"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12383"] :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=\\left\\langle z+2y, \\: 3y+z, \\: x -z\\right\\rangle$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=-3x+2y$ for $0 \\leq x \\leq 2$ and $0 \\leq y \\leq 1.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/assets/3761b12939f74f1e7f4d01ca83ea2884c1296672e22128064b109f7c42bb4df6.png)\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle u,\\: v,\\: -3u+2v \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (u,v) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq u \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq v \\leq 1 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-3u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-3⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-3u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z+2y,\\,3y+z,\\,x-z⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=-3u+2v} \\\\  & =⟨(-3u+2v)+2v,\\,3v+(-3u+2v),\\,u-(-3u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3u+4v,\\,-3u+5v,\\,4u-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-3u+4v,\\,-3u+5v,\\,4u-2v⟩\\cdot ⟨3,\\,-2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(-3u+4v)\\cdot (3)+(-3u+5v)\\cdot (-2)+(4u-2v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-9u+12v+6u-10v+4u-2v \\\\  & =u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z+2y,\\,3y+z,\\,x-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}u\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${\\color{blue}u}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12387"] :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $y = h(x,z)$ for $(x,z) \\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) = \\left\\langle P,\\: Q,\\: R \\right\\rangle$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \n\\Bigg( \n\\bbox[3pt, border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}} \\dfrac{\\partial h}{\\partial x} \n+ Q \n- \\bbox[3pt, border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}} \\dfrac{\\partial h}{\\partial z}\n\\Bigg) \\: \\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?\n\n*Hint: The orientation of $S$ should be chosen such that the unit normal vector has a positive  $\\mathbf j$-component.*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $y = h(x,z),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(x,z) = \\left\\langle x, \\: h(x,z),\\: z \\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂x},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨0,\\frac{∂h}{∂z},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & \\frac{∂h}{∂x} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{∂h}{∂z} & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨\\frac{∂h}{∂x},\\,-1,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂z}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, notice that the $\\mathbf j$-component is negative. Therefore, we select the normal vector that points in the *opposite* direction:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}'_z \\times \\mathbf{r}'_x = - \\mathbf{r}'_x \\times \\mathbf{r}'_z =   \\left \\langle -\\dfrac{\\partial h}{\\partial x}, \\: 1, \\: -\\dfrac{\\partial h}{\\partial z} \\right \\rangle\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,z))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{∂h}{∂x},\\,1,\\,-\\frac{∂h}{∂z}⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂h}{∂x}+Q-R\\frac{∂h}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12357"] :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x, y, z) = \\left\\langle -y, \\: x, \\: z+2 \\right\\rangle,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=x^2+y^2$ for $0 \\leq x \\leq 1$ and $0 \\leq y \\leq 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z = g(x,y)$ for $(x,y) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) = \\left\\langle P,\\: Q,\\: R \\right\\rangle$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\left( -P\\dfrac{\\partial g}{\\partial x} - Q\\dfrac{\\partial g}{\\partial y} + R \\right) \\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2x \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $\\mathbf F(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨-y,\\,x,\\,z+2⟩{|}_{z={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨{{-y}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{x}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨-y,\\,x,\\,z+2⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-(-y)\\cdot (2x)-(x)\\cdot (2y)+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2xy-2xy+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{x}^{2}y+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+2y]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+\\frac{7}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{7x}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{7}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
